==Trivia==
{| class="fandom-table"
|'''General'''
* It is recommended to use close-ranged fruits like [[Portal]] to increase combo effectiveness instead of using long ranged [[Blox Fruits]] like [[Lightning]].
* The Shark Anchor is the third water-related sword, the first being [[Trident]] and the second being [[Dragon Trident]].
* The Shark Anchor's M1s have a similar sound and VFX to that of [[Sharkman Karate]] and [[Water Kung Fu]]. This does not mean that the M1s do not have any delays.
* The Shark Anchor has the same holding animation as the [[Hallow Scythe]].
|-
|'''[Z] Typhoon Toss'''
* When used near a wall, gold marks will appear on the wall.
* Acts quite similar to [[Cursed Dual Katana]]'s [Z] and awakened [[Dough]]'s [C] move.
* Aiming this move at the ground instead of away will briefly stun the enemy, making [[combos]] easier and more damaging.
|-
|'''[X] Armor Breaker'''
* This move increases the damage on a large enemy, but that does not mean it completely ignores the defense of some transformed fruits. (Such as [[Buddha]], the untransformed user will take 300 damage with one [[Stats|stat]] level, but in the transformed form it is reduced to 200.)
* Interestingly, Transformed [[Phoenix]], [[Venom]], [[Tiger]], and [[Dragon#Transformed (East)|Eastern Dragon]] users do not trigger the special effect of its '''[X] Armor Breaker'''.
|}

